    art: 
    arrival: 'Cornelia: Cornelia Vane-Hartley. I require a mirror. A fire would be
      civilised.

      And keep those rattling things away. I will not share a wall
      with a poltergeist.'
    story:
    - 'Cornelia: Lady Ashworth stole my seat at the Winter Ball of 1881. I have not
      forgotten.'
    - 'Cornelia[sad]: I found her old dance card. She wrote my name on it, then crossed
      it out. Why?'
    - 'Cornelia[happy]: She meant to ask ME to dance, the silly thing, and lost her
      nerve. A hundred and forty years of sulking, wasted.'
    checkout: 'Cornelia[happy]: Take the dance card. And if you see Ashworth, tell
      her... the next waltz is hers.'
    keepsake: Dance Card
